{
  "id": "COMPOUND:34436 - PROTEIN:5829",
  "verbalization": "Lobechinenoid D is shown to interact with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, a protein that is a target of multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. These compounds are both implicated in the target of Lobechinenoid D, and all of them ultimately target CHP-134. This suggests a potential mechanism where Lobechinenoid D may inhibit the activity of the sialyltransferase enzyme, which is a key step in the biosynthesis of sialic acid. The presence of multiple pathways converging on CHP-134 indicates that the sialyltransferase enzyme may be a critical target for Lobechinenoid D, and that the observed interactions may be mediated through this enzyme. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Lobechinenoid D and CHP-134, particularly through the inhibition of a shared target enzyme.",
